---
type Props = { city?: string };
const { city } = Astro.props;
const where = city ? ` in ${city}` : " in Georgia";
---

<h2>Insurance{where}</h2>
<p>
  Sudden pipe bursts and appliance failures are often covered. Slow leaks you
  ignored, flood from a creek or street, and sewer backup may not be — unless
  you bought those add-ons. Only your policy answers that. We do not bill
  insurance. The restoration company can.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Photograph every room before you throw things away.</li>
  <li>Keep a list of damaged items. Do not toss a soaked sofa until they say so, if you can stand the smell.</li>
  <li>Call your carrier when you can. A crew that works insurance jobs will talk to the adjuster.</li>
  <li>Do not start demo if you plan to file. Cutting drywall “to help” can complicate the claim.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  More on first-hour photos and what to move is on
  <a href="/what-to-do">what to do first</a> and
  <a href="/insurance">insurance</a>.
</p>
